senses.gloss:
Dhṛtarāṣṭra (in mg. 1 and 2 = Pali Dhataraṭṭha),
(1) n. of one of the four ‘world-guardians’, see mahārāja(n); guardian of the east and lord of gandharvas;
(2) (see s.v. dhṛtarājya) n. of a haṃsa-king (previous birth of the Bodhisattva): Gv 〔399.26〕; Jm 〔127.24〕; also n. of the haṃsa-king in the story which = the Pali Nacca Jātaka (32), MSV 〔ii.92.17 ff.〕;
(3) n. of a former Buddha, or (probably) of two such: Mv 〔i.138.1〕; 〔iii.235.1〕;
(4) n. of one of Śuddhodanaʼs palaces: LV 〔49.1〕; Mv 〔ii.5.5 ff.〕
